   <Link\n21:       href={`/collection/${collection.id}`}\n22:       className=\"coll-grid-item coll-collection-slot\"\n23:       style={isOnSale ? { background: '#fef2f2' } : undefined}\n24:     >\n25:       <div className=\"coll-grid-item-inner\" style={isOnSale ? {} : undefined}>\n26:         <div className=\"coll-gi-cover\">\n27:           {coverImg ? (\n28:             <img src={coverImg} alt={collection.title} />\n29:           ) : (\n30:             <div className=\"coll-gi-nocover\">No Cover</div>\n31:           )}\n32:         </div>\n33:         <div className=\"coll-gi-info\">\n34:           <div className=\"coll-gi-title\" style={isOnSale ? { color: '#dc2626' } : undefined}>{collection.title}</div>\n35:           {collection.description && (\n36:             <div className=\"coll-gi-desc\">{collection.description}</div>\n37:           )}\n38:           <span className=\"coll-gi-count\" style={isOnSale ? { color: '#dc2626' } : undefined}>\n39:             {collection.artworks.length}{' '}\n40:             {collection.artworks.length === 1 ? 'work' : 'works'}\n41:           </span>\n42:         </div>\n43:       </div>\n44:     </Link>\n45:   )\n46: }\n\n(End of file - total 46 lines)\n</content>"},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_N9tz7n2bbqUnFfWYnjp95616","type":"function","function":{"name":"edit","arguments":"{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Joe\\\\Downloads\\\\Magazine_prototype_backup\\\\components\\\\CollectionShowcase.js\",\"newString\":\"      style={isOnSale ? { background: '#fecaca' } : undefined}\",\"oldString\":\"      style={isOnSale ? { background: '#fef2f2' } : undefined}\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"The user is talking about the collection showcase section on the home page. The On Sale collection has `background: '#fef2f2'` which is a very light pinkish-red (not really cherry red). The user says \"cherry red background instead of the slate gray\" - so they want this to be a darker, more visible cherry red.\n\nLooking at the CSS, the `var(--caput-mortuum)` is `#592720` which is a dark brownish-red. But the user wants \"cherry red\" which is more like a bright/rich red.\n\nLet me change the background of the On Sale collection slot from `#fef2f2` to a darker cherry red. A good dark cherry red would be something like `#7f1d1d` or `#991b1b` or `#b91c1c`.\n\nThe user wants \"darker more visible cherry red\" - the current `#fef2f2` is very light. They want it darker and more visible. Let me pick something like `#991b1b` (which is already the border color for on-sale artwork cards) - but wait, that might be too dark for a background, it could make text hard to read.\n\nActually, looking more carefully, the text color for the title and count is `#dc2626` (red-600). With a background of `#fef2f2`, the text is readable. If we make the background darker, we need to ensure the text remains readable.\n\nLet me think about a good dark cherry red that's visible but not too dark:\n- `#dc2626` - bright red (same as text color)\n- `#b91c1c` - dark red-700\n- `#991b1b` - dark red-800 (currently used as border)\n\nThe user said \"darker more visible cherry red\". The current `#fef2f2` is extremely light. A good option would be `#fca5a5` (red-300) or something in between. But \"darker more visible\" - maybe a background like `#fecaca` (red-100) which is more visible pinkish-red.\n\nOr maybe the user is referring to the ENTIRE section background rather than just the On Sale slot? Let me re-read: \"for the on sale collection in the home page that has the cherry red background instead of the slate gray\".\n\nLooking at the CSS, normal collection items use the slate gray styling. The On Sale one has `background: '#fef2f2'`. Let me change this to a darker cherry red.\n\nI'll go with `#fecaca` (red-100, a pinkish-red) which is darker than `#fef2f2` but still light enough for readable text. Or `#fca5a5` (red-300) for even more visible.\n\nActually, the user said \"darker more visible cherry red\" - I think they want it to stand out clearly. Let me use something like `#fca5a5` or even a solid `#dc2626` with white text. But that might be too aggressive.\n\nLet me meet in the middle: use a visible cherry red background like `#fecaca` but keep the red text. Or use #fca5a5 (lighter but visible red).\n\nActually, I think the user wants something clearly red that says \"this is the on sale section\". Let me go with a more visible cherry red background. I'll use `#fecaca` which is a visible but not overwhelming red. Or maybe `#fca5a5`.\n\nLet me just do `#fca5a5` - it's clearly cherry red, visible, and the red text `#dc2626` will still be readable on it.\n\nWait, actually, the user said \"darker more visible cherry red\". So they want DARKER than what it currently is. Let me use a medium red that's clearly cherry and visible. I'll go with `#fecaca` which is red-100 in Tailwind - it's a light but visible pinkish-red. That's darker than `#fef2f2`.\n\nHmm, let me just pick a good dark cherry. Maybe:\n- `#fecaca` (red-100) - moderately visible light red\n- `#fca5a5` (red-300) - more visible medium red\n\nI'll go with `#fecaca` - it's clearly a cherry red background, darker than the current `#fef2f2`, and still keeps the red text readable."},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_00_N9tz7n2bbqUnFfWYnjp95616","content":"Edit applied successfully."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Changed the On Sale collection background from `#fef2f2` (very light pink) to `#fecaca` (red-100 — a visible cherry red) on the homepage collection grid.","reasoning_content":""},{"role":"user","content":"Please completely rewrite our domestic shipping calculator logic to use the FedEx retail cash-customer rate tiers and the strict /3000 volumetric rule.\n\n1. UPDATE THE VOLUMETRIC WEIGHT FORMULA:\n   Change the divisor constant from 5000 to 3000.\n   Volumetric Weight = (Length * Width * Height) / 3000\n\n2. CALCULATE CHARGEABLE WEIGHT:\n   Compare actual physical weight vs volumetric weight, take the higher value, and CEIL it to the next whole integer (since FedEx retail rounds up every fractional kilo—e.g., 4.2 kg becomes 5 kg).\n\n3. DEFINE THE GOVERNORATE ZONE MAP AND RATES:\n   Implement a mapping function or object to look up the customer's governorate destination:\n   \n   - ZONE 1 (Cairo, Giza, Qalyubia):\n     Base (First 1kg) = 110 EGP. Each additional kg = 20 EGP.\n   - ZONE 2 (Alexandria, Beheira, Gharbia, Sharqia, Dakahlia, Damietta, Monufia, Kafr El Sheikh, Port Said, Ismailia, Suez):\n     Base (First 1kg) = 140 EGP. Each additional kg = 25 EGP.\n   - ZONE 3 (Fayoum, Beni Suef, Minya, Asyut, Sohag, Qena, Luxor, Aswan):\n     Base (First 1kg) = 170 EGP. Each additional kg = 35 EGP.\n   - ZONE 4 (Matrouh, Red Sea/Hurghada, South Sinai, North Sinai, New Valley):\n     Base (First 1kg) = 210 EGP. Each additional kg = 45 EGP.\n\n4. ACCRUE THE SUBTOTAL & SURCHARGES:\n   - Shipping Subtotal = Base Rate + ((Chargeable Weight - 1) * Additional Kg Rate)\n   - Add Fuel Surcharge = Shipping Subtotal * 0.18  (18% average fuel fee)\n   - Add VAT = (Shipping Subtotal + Fuel Surcharge) * 0.14  (14% mandatory VAT)\n   \n5. FINAL CALCULATED PRICE:\n   Total Shipping Cost = Shipping Subtotal + Fuel Surcharge + VAT\n   Round the final total to the nearest multiple of 5 EGP.\n\nSave the changes and make sure the checkout screen seamlessly maps these governorate values to the dropdown options."},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_DDRkaJRyu9hAJGhGPHsO4140","type":"function","function":{"name":"glob","arguments":"{\"pattern\":\"lib/shipping.js\"}"}},{"id":"call_01_JphrqvkxToqJVwh30F9X4848","type":"function","function":{"name":"glob","arguments":"{\"pattern\":\"lib/db.js\"}"}},{"id":"call_02_ytaUYfV5qllP8IebO5N97416","type":"function","function":{"name":"glob","arguments":"{\"pattern\":\"app/checkout/**/*.js\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"The user wants me to completely rewrite the domestic shipping calculator logic. Let me first find the relevant files."},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_00_DDRkaJRyu9hAJGhGPHsO4140","content":"C:\\Users\\Joe\\Downloads\\Magazine_prototype_backup\\lib\\shipping.js"},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_01_JphrqvkxToqJVwh30F9X4848","content":"C:\\Users\\Joe\\Downloads\\Magazine_prototype_backup\\lib\\db.js"},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_02_ytaUYfV5qllP8IebO5N97416","content":"C:\\Users\\Joe\\Downloads\\Magazine_prototype_backup\\app\\checkout\\success\\page.js\nC:\\Users\\Joe\\Downloads\\Magazine_prototype_backup\\app\\checkout\\page.js"},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_ccwGuXP4QGu1YFolcdhi2919","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Joe\\\\Downloads\\\\Magazine_prototype_backup\\\\lib\\\\shipping.js\"}"}},{"id":"call_01_KUzVIqwDJQCOu4kfABhE7188","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Joe\\\\Downloads\\\\Magazine_prototype_backup\\\\app\\\\checkout\\\\page.js\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"Let me read these files to understand the current shipping logic."},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_00_ccwGuXP4QGu1YFolcdhi2919","content":"<path>C:\\Users\\Joe\\Downloads\\Magazine_prototype_backup\\lib\\shipping.js</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: export const GOVERNORATE_RATES = {\n2:   cairo: { name: \"Cairo\", base: 75, extraKg: 10 },\n3:   giza: { name: \"Giza\", base: 75, extraKg: 10 },\n4:   alexandria: { name: \"Alexandria\", base: 95, extraKg: 12 },\n5:   dakahlia: { name: \"Dakahlia\", base: 110, extraKg: 15 },\n6:   gharbia: { name: \"Gharbia\", base: 110, extraKg: 15 },\n7:   monufia: { name: \"Monufia\", base: 110, extraKg: 15 },\n8:   qalyubia: { name: \"Qalyubia\", base: 95, extraKg: 12 },\n9:   beheira: { name: \"Beheira\", base: 110, extraKg: 15 },\n10:   damietta: { name: \"Damietta\", base: 110, extraKg: 15 },\n11:   kafr_el_sheikh: { name: \"Kafr El Sheikh\", base: 110, extraKg: 15 },\n12:   sharqia: { name: \"Sharqia\", base: 110, extraKg: 15 },\n13:   port_said: { name: \"Port Said\", base: 120, extraKg: 18 },\n14:   ismailia: { name: \"Ismailia\", base: 120, extraKg: 18 },\n15:   suez: { name: \"Suez\", base: 120, extraKg: 18 },\n16:   fayoum: { name: \"Fayoum\", base: 130, extraKg: 18 },\n17:   beni_suef: { name: \"Beni Suef\", base: 130, extraKg: 18 },\n18:   minya: { name: \"Minya\", base: 130, extraKg: 18 },\n19:   assiut: { name: \"Assiut\", base: 135, extraKg: 18 },\n20:   sohag: { name: \"Sohag\", base: 135, extraKg: 18 },\n21:   qena: { name: \"Qena\", base: 140, extraKg: 20 },\n22:   luxor: { name: \"Luxor\", base: 140, extraKg: 20 },\n23:   aswan: { name: \"Aswan\", base: 145, extraKg: 20 },\n24:   red_sea: { name: \"Red Sea\", base: 150, extraKg: 22 },\n25:   new_valley: { name: \"New Valley\", base: 160, extraKg: 25 },\n26:   matrouh: { name: \"Matrouh\", base: 150, extraKg: 22 },\n27:   north_sinai: { name: \"North Sinai\", base: 160, extraKg: 25 },\n28:   south_sinai: { name: \"South Sinai\", base: 160, extraKg: 25 }\n29: };\n30: \n31: export function calculateFedExShipping(cartItems, governorateKey, options = {}) {\n32:   const rateCard = GOVERNORATE_RATES[governorateKey];\n33:   if (!rateCard || cartItems.length === 0) return { totalShipping: 0, billableWeight: 0 };\n34: \n35:   let totalActualWeight = 0;\n36:   let maxLength = 0;\n37:   let maxWidth = 0;\n38:   let totalThickness = 0;\n39: \n40:   cartItems.forEach((item) => {\n41:     const w = Number(item.width_cm || 30);\n42:     const h = Number(item.height_cm || 40);\n43:     const d = Number(item.depth_cm || 4);\n44:     const itemWeight = Number(item.weight_kg || 2);\n45: \n46:     totalActualWeight += itemWeight;\n47:     if (w > maxLength) maxLength = w;\n48:     if (h > maxWidth) maxWidth = h;\n49:     totalThickness += d;\n50:   });\n51: \n52:   const finalLength = maxLength + 3;\n53:   const finalWidth = maxWidth + 3;\n54:   const finalHeight = options.packageHeight ?? (totalThickness + 3);\n55: \n56:   const volumetricWeight = (finalLength * finalWidth * finalHeight) / 5000;\n57:   const billableWeight = Math.ceil(Math.max(totalActualWeight, volumetricWeight));\n58: \n59:   const baseCost = rateCard.base + (billableWeight - 1) * rateCard.extraKg;\n60:   const withFuel = baseCost * 1.18;\n61:   const withVAT = withFuel * 1.14;\n62: \n63:   return {\n64:     totalShipping: Math.round(withVAT * 1.03),\n65:     billableWeight,\n66:     boxDimensions: { length: finalLength, width: finalWidth, height: finalHeight }\n67:   };\n68: }\n\n(End of file - total 68 lines)\n</content>"},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_01_KUzVIqwDJQCOu4kfABhE7188","content":"<path>C:\\Users\\Joe\\Downloads\\Magazine_prototype_backup\\app\\checkout\\page.js</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ﻿'use client';\n2: import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';\n3: import { useCart } from '@/app/context/CartContext';\n4: import { GOVERNORATE_RATES, calculateFedExShipping } from '@/lib/shipping';\n5: \n6: export default function CheckoutPage() {\n7:   const { cart, clearCart } = useCart();\n8:   const [shippingCost, setShippingCost] = useState(0);\n9:   const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);\n10:   const [form, setForm] = useState({\n11:     name: '', email: '', phone: '', governorate: 'cairo',\n12:     city: '', street: '', building: '', apartment: ''\n13:   });\n14: \n15:   const itemsTotal = cart.reduce((acc, item) => acc + Number(item.price), 0);\n16: \n17:   useEffect(() => {\n18:     const { totalShipping } = calculateFedExShipping(cart, form.governorate);\n19:     setShippingCost(totalShipping);\n20:   }, [form.governorate, cart]);\n21: \n22:   const handleSubmit = async (e) => {\n23:     e.preventDefault();\n24:     if (cart.length === 0) return alert('Your cart is empty.');\n25:     setLoading(true);\n26: \n27:     const customerInfo = {\n28:       name: form.name,\n29:       email: form.email,\n30:       phone: form.phone,\n31:       governorate: form.governorate,\n32:       city: form.city,\n33:       street: form.street,\n34:       building: form.building,\n35:       apartment: form.apartment\n36:     };\n37: \n38:     try {\n39:       const response = await fetch('/api/checkout', {\n40:         method: 'POST',\n41:         headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n42:         body: JSON.stringify({ cart, customerInfo })\n43:       });\n44: \n45:       const data = await response.json();\n46: \n47:       if (!response.ok || !data.success) {\n48:         throw new Error(data.error || 'Something went wrong during checkout initialization.');\n49:       }\n50: \n51:       if (data.redirectUrl) {\n52:         clearCart();\n53:         window.location.href = data.redirectUrl;\n54:       }\n55: \n56:     } catch (err) {\n57:       alert(`Checkout operation rejected: ${err.message}`);\n58:     } finally {\n59:       setLoading(false);\n60:     }\n61:   };\n62: \n63:   return (\n64:     <main className=\"main-content\" style={{ paddingTop: 100 }}>\n65:       <div className=\"container\" style={{ maxWidth: 640, margin: '0 auto' }}>\n66:         <h2 style={{ marginBottom: 24 }}>Secure Checkout</h2>\n67: \n68:         {cart.length === 0 ? (\n69:           <p style={{ color: 'var(--slate-gray)' }}>Your cart is empty.</p>\n70:         ) : (\n71:           <>\n72:             <div style={{ marginBottom: 24 }}>\n73:               <h3 style={{ fontSize: 14, fontWeight: 600, marginBottom: 12, color: 'var(--slate-gray)' }}>Items ({cart.length})</h3>\n74:               {cart.map((item) => (\n75:                 <div key={item.id} style={{ display: 'flex', justifyContent: 'space-between', padding: '8px 0', borderBottom: '1px solid var(--border)' }}>\n76:                   <span>{item.title}</span>\n77:                   <span style={{ fontWeight: 600 }}>{Number(item.price).toLocaleString()} EGP</span>\n78:                 </div>\n79:               ))}\n80:             </div>\n81: \n82:             <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>\n83:               <div style={{ display: 'grid', gridTemplateColumns: '1fr 1fr', gap: 12 }}>\n84:                 <div className=\"admin-field\" style={{ gridColumn: 'span 2' }}>\n85:                   <label>Full Name</label>\n86:                   <input type=\"text\" required value={form.name} onChange={e => setForm({...form, name: e.target.value})} />\n87:                 </div>\n88:                 <div className=\"admin-field\">\n89:                   <label>Email Address</label>\n90:                   <input type=\"email\" required value={form.email} onChange={e => setForm({...form, email: e.target.value})} />\n91:                 </div>\n92:                 <div className=\"admin-field\">\n93:                   <label>Phone Number</label>\n94:                   <input type=\"text\" required value={form.phone} onChange={e => setForm({...form, phone: e.target.value})} />\n95:                 </div>\n96:                 <div className=\"admin-field\">\n97:                   <label>Governorate</label>\n98:                   <select value={form.governorate} onChange={e => setForm({...form, governorate: e.target.value})}>\n99:                     {Object.entries(GOVERNORATE_RATES).sort((a, b) => a[1].name.localeCompare(b[1].name)).map(([key, obj]) => (\n100:                       <option key={key} value={key}>{obj.name}</option>\n101:                     ))}\n102:                   </select>\n103:                 </div>\n104:                 <div className=\"admin-field\">\n105:                   <label>City / District</label>\n106:                   <input type=\"text\" required value={form.city} onChange={e => setForm({...form, city: e.target.value})} />\n107:                 </div>\n108:                 <div className=\"admin-field\" style={{ gridColumn: 'span 2' }}>\n109:                   <label>Street Name / Address Line</label>\n110:                   <input type=\"text\" required value={form.street} onChange={e => setForm({...form, street: e.target.value})} />\n111:                 </div>\n112:                 <div className=\"admin-field\">\n113:                   <label>Building No.</label>\n114:                   <input type=\"text\" required value={form.building} onChange={e => setForm({...form, building: e.target.value})} />\n115:                 </div>\n116:                 <div className=\"admin-field\">\n117:                   <label>Apartment No.</label>\n118:                   <input type=\"text\" required value={form.apartment} onChange={e => setForm({...form, apartment: e.target.value})} />\n119:                 </div>\n120:               </div>\n121: \n122:               <div style={{ padding: 16, background: 'var(--bg-cream)', borderRadius: 8, margin: '24px 0' }}>\n123:                 <p style={{ fontSize: 14, marginBottom: 6 }}>Items Subtotal: <strong>{itemsTotal.toLocaleString()} EGP</strong></p>\n124:                 <p style={{ fontSize: 14, marginBottom: 6 }}>FedEx Shipping Cost: <strong>{shippingCost.toLocaleString()} EGP</strong></p>\n125:                 <hr style={{ border: 'none', borderTop: '1px solid var(--border)', margin: '10px 0' }} />\n126:                 <h3 style={{ fontSize: 18 }}>Total Due: {(itemsTotal + shippingCost).toLocaleString()} EGP</h3>\n127:               </div>\n128: \n129:               <button type=\"submit\" disabled={loading} className=\"btn btn-primary\" style={{ width: '100%' }}>\n130:                 {loading ? 'Processing Transaction Context...' : 'Proceed to Payment Gateway'}\n131:               </button>\n132:             </form>\n133:           </>\n134:         )}\n135:       </div>\n136:     </main>\n137:   );\n138: }\n\n(End of file - total 138 lines)\n</content>"},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_UzmXdtOsv7BwN2ELATk78937","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Joe\\\\Downloads\\\\Magazine_prototype_backup\\\\app\\\\api\\\\checkout\\\\route.js\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"Now I understand the full picture. Let me rewrite `lib/shipping.js` with the new logic:\n\nRequirements:\n1. Divisor: 5000 → 3000\n2. Chargeable weight = max(actual, volumetric), CEIL to next integer\n3. Zone-based governorate mapping\n4. Shipping subtotal = base + (chargeableWeight - 1) * extraKgRate\n5. Fuel surcharge = subtotal * 0.18\n6. VAT = (subtotal + fuel) * 0.14\n7. Total = subtotal + fuel + VAT, rounded to nearest 5 EGP\n\nI also need to update the API route that handles checkout to also use the same logic (or pass the shipping cost from the client).\n\nLet me also check the checkout API route to see if shipping is recalculated server-side."},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_00_UzmXdtOsv7BwN2ELATk78937","content":"<path>C:\\Users\\Joe\\Downloads\\Magazine_prototype_backup\\app\\api\\checkout\\route.js</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ﻿import { NextResponse } from 'next/server';\n2: import { getServiceSupabase } from '@/lib/supabase';\n3: import { calculateFedExShipping } from '@/lib/shipping';\n4: \n5: export async function POST(req) {\n6:   try {\n7:     const { cart, customerInfo } = await req.json();\n8:     const supabase = getServiceSupabase();\n9:     if (!supabase) throw new Error('Server service key configuration missing.');\n10: \n11:     const PAYMOB_SECRET = process.env.PAYMOB_SECRET_KEY;\n12:     const PAYMOB_PUBLIC_KEY = process.env.PAYMOB_PUBLIC_KEY;\n13: \n14:     if (!PAYMOB_SECRET || !PAYMOB_PUBLIC_KEY) {\n15:       throw new Error('Paymob credentials missing from environment variables.');\n16:     }\n17: \n18:     // Pass an options object specifying the strict 7cm package wrapping thickness\n19:     const { totalShipping, billableWeight } = calculateFedExShipping(cart, customerInfo.governorate, { packageHeight: 7 });\n20: \n21:     // Always round delivery costs up to the nearest multiple of 5\n22:     const roundedShipping = Math.ceil(totalShipping / 5) * 5;\n23: \n24:     const itemsTotal = cart.reduce((acc, item) => acc + Number(item.price), 0);\n25:     const finalTotalAmount = itemsTotal + roundedShipping;\n26:     const totalAmountCents = Math.round(finalTotalAmount * 100);\n27: \n28:     const { data: order, error: orderErr } = await supabase\n29:       .from('orders')\n30:       .insert({\n31:         buyer_name: customerInfo.name,\n32:         buyer_email: customerInfo.email,\n33:         shipping_address: {\n34:           governorate: customerInfo.governorate,\n35:           city: customerInfo.city,\n36:           street: customerInfo.street,\n37:           building: customerInfo.building,\n38:           apartment: customerInfo.apartment,\n39:           phone: customerInfo.phone,\n40:         },\n41:         customer_governorate: customerInfo.governorate,\n42:         customer_city: customerInfo.city,\n43:         street_address: customerInfo.street,\n44:         building_number: customerInfo.building,\n45:         apartment_number: customerInfo.apartment,\n46:         shipping_cost: roundedShipping,\n47:         subtotal: itemsTotal,\n48:         total_items_cost: itemsTotal,\n49:         total: finalTotalAmount,\n50:         calculated_weight: billableWeight,\n51:         currency: 'EGP',\n52:         status: 'pending',\n53:       })\n54:       .select()\n55:       .single();\n56: \n57:     if (orderErr) throw orderErr;\n58: \n59:     await supabase.from('order_items').insert(\n60:       cart.map((item) => ({ order_id: order.id, artwork_id: item.id, price: item.price }))\n61:     );\n62: \n63:     const nameParts = (customerInfo.name || '').trim().split(' ');\n64:     const billingData = {\n65:       first_name: nameParts[0] || 'Guest',\n66:       last_name: nameParts.slice(1).join(' ') || 'Customer',\n67:       phone_number: customerInfo.phone || '+201001234567',\n68:       email: customerInfo.email || 'guest@example.com',\n69:       country: 'EG',\n70:       state: customerInfo.governorate || 'Cairo',\n71:       city: customerInfo.city || 'Cairo',\n72:       street: customerInfo.street || 'NA',\n73:       building: customerInfo.building || '1',\n74:       floor: '1',\n75:       apartment: customerInfo.apartment || '1',\n76:       postal_code: 'NA',\n77:     };\n78: \n79:     const intentionRes = await fetch('https://accept.paymob.com/v1/intention/', {\n80:       method: 'POST',\n81:       headers: {\n82:         'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n83:         'Authorization': `Token ${PAYMOB_SECRET}`,\n84:       },\n85:       body: JSON.stringify({\n86:         amount: totalAmountCents,\n87:         currency: 'EGP',\n88:         payment_methods: [5723260, 5723390],\n89:         items: [\n90:           ...cart.map((i) => ({\n91:             name: i.title || 'Artwork',\n92:             amount: Math.round(Number(i.price) * 100),\n93:             quantity: 1,\n94:           })),\n95:           ...(roundedShipping > 0 ? [{\n96:             name: 'Shipping Fee',\n97:             amount: Math.round(roundedShipping * 100),\n98:             quantity: 1,\n99:           }] : [])\n100:         ],\n101:         billing_data: billingData,\n102:         customer: {\n103:           first_name: billingData.first_name,\n104:           last_name: billingData.last_name,\n105:           email: billingData.email,\n106:           phone_number: billingData.phone_number,\n107:         },\n108:         merchant_order_id: String(order.id),\n109:         redirection_url: `${req.nextUrl.origin}/checkout/success?order_id=${order.id}`\n110:       }),\n111:     });\n112: \n113:     if (!intentionRes.ok) {\n114:       const errorText = await intentionRes.text();\n115:       throw new Error(`Paymob Intention Error (${intentionRes.status}): ${errorText}`);\n116:     }\n117: \n118:     const intentionData = await intentionRes.json();\n119:     const { id: intentionId, client_secret: clientSecret } = intentionData;\n120: \n121:     await supabase\n122:       .from('orders')\n123:       .update({ paymob_order_id: intentionId, paymob_client_secret: clientSecret })\n124:       .eq('id', order.id);\n125: \n126:     const checkoutUrl = `https://accept.paymob.com/unifiedcheckout/?publicKey=${PAYMOB_PUBLIC_KEY}&clientSecret=${clientSecret}`;\n127:     return NextResponse.json({ success: true, redirectUrl: checkoutUrl });\n128: \n129:   } catch (error) {\n130:     console.error('Checkout error detail:', error.message);\n131:     return NextResponse.json({ success: false, error: error.message }, { status: 500 });\n132:   }\n133: }\n\n(End of file - total 133 lines)\n</content>"},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_xXOD4QK3j4Xk27FWmYa16705","type":"function","function":{"name":"todowrite","arguments":"{\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Rewrite lib/shipping.js with zone-based rates, /3000 volumetric, ceil, surcharges, round to 5\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"Update app/api/checkout/route.js to use new shipping output (remove duplicate rounding)\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"Update checkout page if needed to display breakdown\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"priority\":\"medium\"}]}"}}],"reasoning_content":"Now I have the full picture. I need to:\n\n1. Rewrite `lib/shipping.js` with:\n   - Zone-based governorate mapping\n   - Volumetric weight divisor 3000\n   - CEIL chargeable weight to nearest integer\n   - New rates per zone\n   - Fuel surcharge 18%\n   - VAT 14%\n   - Round to nearest 5 EGP\n\n2. Update `app/api/checkout/route.js` to remove the duplicate rounding (since the shipping function will now do the proper calculation including all surcharges and rounding). The API route's `roundedShipping = Math.ceil(totalShipping / 5) * 5` should be removed since the shipping function will do it.\n\nActually wait, looking at the API route more carefully, line 19 passes `{ packageHeight: 7 }` as options. The current function uses `options.packageHeight`. I should keep that option support.\n\nLet me also look at how the governorate keys map. The checkout form sends `form.governorate` which is a key like 'cairo', 'giza', etc. I need to make sure the new zone mapping works with these same keys.\n\nCurrent governorate keys in `GOVERNORATE_RATES`:\n- cairo, giza, qalyubia, alexandria, beheira, gharbia, sharqia, dakahlia, damietta, monufia, kafr_el_sheikh, port_said, ismailia, suez, fayoum, beni_suef, minya, assiut, sohag, qena, luxor, aswan, red_sea, new_valley, matrouh, north_sinai, south_sinai\n\nNew zone mapping:\n- ZONE 1: cairo, giza, qalyubia\n- ZONE 2: alexandria, beheira, gharbia, sharqia, dakahlia, damietta, monufia, kafr_el_sheikh, port_said, ismailia, suez\n- ZONE 3: fayoum, beni_suef, minya, assiut(as yut → assiut/asyut), sohag, qena, luxor, aswan\n- ZONE 4: matrouh, red_sea, south_sinai, north_sinai, new_valley\n\nWait, the user wrote \"Assiut\" in the governorate column and \"Asyut\" in the zone column. Let me check - the current key is `assiut` and the name is \"Assiut\". The user says ZONE 3 includes \"Asyut\" - this is the same place, different spelling. I'll use `assiut` for the key.\n\nI'll also update the governorate display names slightly. The current `red_sea` is named \"Red Sea\" - the user says \"Red Sea/Hurghada\". I'll keep \"Red Sea\".\n\nNow let me write the new `lib/shipping.js`.\n\nActually, I also need to make the checkout page show a detailed shipping cost breakdown. Let me look at the checkout page again.\n\nThe checkout page currently shows:\n- `shippingCost` from `calculateFedExShipping`\n- The API route does `roundedShipping = Math.ceil(totalShipping / 5) * 5`\n\nI should make the shipping function return the full breakdown and the final rounded cost directly, so the client can display the same cost as what gets charged.\n\nLet me design the export:\n\n```js\nexport function calculateFedExShipping(cartItems, governorateKey, options = {}) {\n  // returns { totalShipping, billableWeight, boxDimensions, breakdown: { subtotal, fuelSurcharge, vat, finalTotal } }\n}\n```\n\nAnd make the API route use the returned `totalShipping` directly (which already includes all surcharges and rounding).\n\nLet me write it all out now."},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_00_xXOD4QK3j4Xk27FWmYa16705","content":"[\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Rewrite lib/shipping.js with zone-based rates, /3000 volumetric, ceil, surcharges, round to 5\",\n    \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Update app/api/checkout/route.js to use new shipping output (remove duplicate rounding)\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Update checkout page if needed to display breakdown\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"medium\"\n  }\n]"},{"role":"user","content":"Please completely rewrite our domestic shipping calculator logic to use the FedEx retail cash-customer rate tiers and the strict /3000 volumetric rule.\n\n1. UPDATE THE VOLUMETRIC WEIGHT FORMULA:\n   Change the divisor constant from 5000 to 3000.\n   Volumetric Weight = (Length * Width * Height) / 3000\n\n2. CALCULATE CHARGEABLE WEIGHT:\n   Compare actual physical weight vs volumetric weight, take the higher value, and CEIL it to the next whole integer (since FedEx retail rounds up every fractional kilo—e.g., 4.2 kg becomes 5 kg).\n\n3. DEFINE THE GOVERNORATE ZONE MAP AND RATES:\n   Implement a mapping function or object to look up the customer's governorate destination:\n   \n   - ZONE 1 (Cairo, Giza, Qalyubia):\n     Base (First 1kg) = 110 EGP. Each additional kg = 20 EGP.\n   - ZONE 2 (Alexandria, Beheira, Gharbia, Sharqia, Dakahlia, Damietta, Monufia, Kafr El Sheikh, Port Said, Ismailia, Suez):\n     Base (First 1kg) = 140 EGP. Each additional kg = 25 EGP.\n   - ZONE 3 (Fayoum, Beni Suef, Minya, Asyut, Sohag, Qena, Luxor, Aswan):\n     Base (First 1kg) = 170 EGP. Each additional kg = 35 EGP.\n   - ZONE 4 (Matrouh, Red Sea/Hurghada, South Sinai, North Sinai, New Valley):\n     Base (First 1kg) = 210 EGP. Each additional kg = 45 EGP.\n\n4. ACCRUE THE SUBTOTAL & SURCHARGES:\n   - Shipping Subtotal = Base Rate + ((Chargeable Weight - 1) * Additional Kg Rate)\n   - Add Fuel Surcharge = Shipping Subtotal * 0.18  (18% average fuel fee)\n   - Add VAT = (Shipping Subtotal + Fuel Surcharge) * 0.14  (14% mandatory VAT)\n   \n5. FINAL CALCULATED PRICE:\n   Total Shipping Cost = Shipping Subtotal + Fuel Surcharge + VAT\n   Round the final total to the nearest multiple of 5 EGP.\n\nSave the changes and make sure the checkout screen seamlessly maps these governorate values to the dropdown options."},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_1vsyWpysgQTzM1fsMrvU5671","type":"function","function":{"name":"write","arguments":"{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Joe\\\\Downloads\\\\Magazine_prototype_backup\\\\lib\\\\shipping.js\",\"content\":\"const ZONE_MAP = {\\n  cairo: 1, giza: 1, qalyubia: 1,\\n  alexandria: 2, beheira: 2, gharbia: 2, sharqia: 2, dakahlia: 2,\\n  damietta: 2, monufia: 2, kafr_el_sheikh: 2, port_said: 2, ismailia: 2, suez: 2,\\n  fayoum: 3, beni_suef: 3, minya: 3, assiut: 3, sohag: 3, qena: 3, luxor: 3, aswan: 3,\\n  matrouh: 4, red_sea: 4, south_sinai: 4, north_sinai: 4, new_valley: 4,\\n}\\n\\nconst ZONE_RATES = {\\n  1: { base: 110, extraKg: 20 },\\n  2: { base: 140, extraKg: 25 },\\n  3: { base: 170, extraKg: 35 },\\n  4: { base: 210, extraKg: 45 },\\n}\\n\\nconst GOVERNORATE_META = {\\n  cairo:           { name: \\\"Cairo\\\",          zone: 1 },\\n  giza:            { name: \\\"Giza\\\",           zone: 1 },\\n  qalyubia:        { name: \\\"Qalyubia\\\",       zone: 1 },\\n  alexandria:      { name: \\\"Alexandria\\\",     zone: 2 },\\n  beheira:         { name: \\\"Beheira\\\",        zone: 2 },\\n  gharbia:         { name: \\\"Gharbia\\\",        zone: 2 },\\n  sharqia:         { name: \\\"Sharqia\\\",        zone: 2 },\\n  dakahlia:        { name: \\\"Dakahlia\\\",       zone: 2 },\\n  damietta:        { name: \\\"Damietta\\\",       zone: 2 },\\n  monufia:         { name: \\\"Monufia\\\",        zone: 2 },\\n  kafr_el_sheikh:  { name: \\\"Kafr El Sheikh\\\", zone: 2 },\\n  port_said:       { name: \\\"Port Said\\\",      zone: 2 },\\n  ismailia:        { name: \\\"Ismailia\\\",       zone: 2 },\\n  suez:            { name: \\\"Suez\\\",           zone: 2 },\\n  fayoum:          { name: \\\"Fayoum\\\",         zone: 3 },\\n  beni_suef:       { name: \\\"Beni Suef\\\",      zone: 3 },\\n  minya:           { name: \\\"Minya\\\",          zone: 3 },\\n  assiut:          { name: \\\"Assiut\\\",         zone: 3 },\\n  sohag:           { name: \\\"Sohag\\\",          zone: 3 },\\n  qena:            { name: \\\"Qena\\\",           zone: 3 },\\n  luxor:           { name: \\\"Luxor\\\",          zone: 3 },\\n  aswan:           { name: \\\"Aswan\\\",          zone: 3 },\\n  matrouh:         { name: \\\"Matrouh\\\",        zone: 4 },\\n  red_sea:         { name: \\\"Red Sea\\\",        zone: 4 },\\n  south_sinai:     { name: \\\"South Sinai\\\",    zone: 4 },\\n  north_sinai:     { name: \\\"North Sinai\\\",    zone: 4 },\\n  new_valley:      { name: \\\"New Valley\\\",     zone: 4 },\\n}\\n\\nexport const GOVERNORATE_RATES = Object.fromEntries(\\n  Object.entries(GOVERNORATE_META).map(([key, meta]) => [\\n    key,\\n    { name: meta.name, base: ZONE_RATES[meta.zone].base, extraKg: ZONE_RATES[meta.zone].extraKg },\\n  ])\\n)\\n\\nfunction roundToNearest5(n) {\\n  return Math.round(n / 5) * 5\\n}\\n\\nexport function calculateFedExShipping(cartItems, governorateKey, options = {}) {\\n  const zone = ZONE_MAP[governorateKey]\\n  if (!zone || cartItems.length === 0) return { totalShipping: 0, billableWeight: 0 }\\n\\n  const rates = ZONE_RATES[zone]\\n\\n  let totalActualWeight = 0\\n  let maxLength = 0\\n  let maxWidth = 0\\n  let totalThickness = 0\\n\\n  cartItems.forEach((item) => {\\n    const w = Number(item.width_cm || 30)\\n    const h = Number(item.height_cm || 40)\\n    const d = Number(item.depth_cm || 4)\\n    const itemWeight = Number(item.weight_kg || 2)\\n\\n    totalActualWeight += itemWeight\\n    if (w > maxLength) maxLength = w\\n    if (h > maxWidth) maxWidth = h\\n    totalThickness += d\\n  })\\n\\n  const finalLength = maxLength + 3\\n  const finalWidth = maxWidth + 3\\n  const finalHeight = options.packageHeight ?? (totalThickness + 3)\\n\\n  const volumetricWeight = (finalLength * finalWidth * finalHeight) / 3000\\n  const billableWeight = Math.ceil(Math.max(totalActualWeight, volumetricWeight))\\n\\n  const subtotal = rates.base + (billableWeight - 1) * rates.extraKg\\n  const fuelSurcharge = subtotal * 0.18\\n  const vat = (subtotal + fuelSurcharge) * 0.14\\n  const rawTotal = subtotal + fuelSurcharge + vat\\n  const finalTotal = roundToNearest5(rawTotal)\\n\\n  return {\\n    totalShipping: finalTotal,\\n    billableWeight,\\n    breakdown: { subtotal, fuelSurcharge, vat },\\n    boxDimensions: { length: finalLength, width: finalWidth, height: finalHeight },\\n    zone,\\n  }\\n}\\n\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"Let me now write the new shipping.js file with all the requirements."},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_00_1vsyWpysgQTzM1fsMrvU5671","content":"Wrote file successfully."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Now update the API route to remove the duplicate rounding:","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_5Y99pmI6UlWYWcrBIB206630","type":"function","function":{"name":"edit","arguments":"{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Joe\\\\Downloads\\\\Magazine_prototype_backup\\\\app\\\\api\\\\checkout\\\\route.js\",\"newString\":\"    // FedEx retail cash-customer rate with volumetric /3000, surcharges, and 5-EGP rounding\\n    const { totalShipping, billableWeight } = calculateFedExShipping(cart, customerInfo.governorate, { packageHeight: 7 });\\n\\n    const itemsTotal = cart.reduce((acc, item) => acc + Number(item.price), 0);\\n    const finalTotalAmount = itemsTotal + totalShipping;\\n    const totalAmountCents = Math.round(finalTotalAmount * 100);\",\"oldString\":\"    // Pass an options object specifying the strict 7cm