et me re-read what the user wants:\n\n```\nrow 1:  img       coll      year       status     .\nrow 2:  img       .         feat       onsale     .\nrow 3:  price     .        Checkbox   checkbox    .\nrow 4:  drag      .         action   .  action        .\n```\n\nAnd also: \"make the checkboxes work and they should apply their function instantly\"\n\nSo I need to:\n1. Update the grid to match this new layout\n2. The \"Checkbox\" and \"checkbox\" on row 3 might be redundant with feat/onsale on row 2... or the user wants feat/onsale on row 2 and the actual checkboxes on row 3? That's confusing.\n3. Row 4 has \"action   .  action\" which seems to split Edit and Delete into separate columns\n4. Make toggleField optimistic (done)\n\nLet me think about what the grid should be. The user is showing a 5-column grid with:\n\nRow 1: img | coll | year | status | .\nRow 2: img | . | feat | onsale | .\nRow 3: price | . | Checkbox | checkbox | .\nRow 4: drag | . | action | . | action\n\nWait, I think the user wants:\n- Row 2: feat and onsale (the checkboxes with labels)\n- Row 3: Checkbox and checkbox (maybe just the checkbox inputs without labels? Or maybe the user is just being redundant/emphasizing?)\n- Row 4: drag, action, and another action (Edit and Delete buttons)\n\nBut having feat/onsale on row 2 AND Checkbox/checkbox on row 3 is weird if they're the same checkboxes. Unless the user wants them on row 3 instead of row 2, and row 2 is empty?\n\nActually, I think the user might be showing the grid with feat/onsale on row 2, and then on row 3 they're just labeling \"these are checkboxes\". Or maybe they want me to interpret \"Checkbox\" and \"checkbox\" as separate things.\n\nYou know what, let me look at this more pragmatically. The user wants:\n1. Collection, Year, Status on row 1 (with Image spanning 2 rows)\n2. Featured and On Sale checkboxes somewhere\n3. Price on its own row\n4. Drag handle and Action buttons on the bottom row\n\nThe user specifically wrote row 2 as \"feat\" and \"onsale\" and row 3 as \"Checkbox\" and \"checkbox\". Maybe feat/onsale on row 2 are the labels, and Checkbox/checkbox on row 3 are the checkbox inputs? That would require splitting each checkbox+label into separate rows, which is complex.\n\nOr maybe the user wants feat and onsale (with their checkboxes) on row 2, and row 3 has something else? But what?\n\nActually, re-reading: \"also make the checkboxes work and they should apply their function instantly\"\n\nThis is the main ask. The grid layout might be showing where things should go, but the key issue is the checkboxes not working/not applying instantly.\n\nOK, I think the best approach is to:\n1. Implement the grid layout the user showed (as closely as I can interpret)\n2. Make the toggleField optimistic (done)\n3. Split the actions td items if needed\n\nLet me try this grid:\n\n```\n\"img   coll  year  status .\"\n\"img   .     feat  onsale .\"\n\"price .     feat  onsale .\"\n\"drag  .     edit  .     delete\"\n```\n\nWait, row 3 has feat and onsale again (spanning from row 2). And \"Checkbox\" / \"checkbox\" is just the user saying \"these are checkboxes\". So feat/onsale span rows 2-3.\n\nAnd for row 4: \"action . action\" means Edit button and Delete button in separate columns. I'll use `display: contents` on the actions td to achieve this.\n\nBut hmm, the user's row 4 says \"action   .  action\" which could mean:\n- col 3: action (Edit)\n- col 4: . (empty)\n- col 5: action (Delete)\n\nSo edit in col 3, delete in col 5, col 4 is empty.\n\nLet me implement this and see. I'll update the grid and CSS.\n\nActually, I realize I need to be careful here. The user's grid says:\n\nRow 2: feat, onsale\nRow 3: Checkbox, checkbox\n\nBut I can't have feat AND Checkbox in the same column on different rows. Unless feat spans rows 2-3 (as a single area spanning both rows). Then both \"feat\" and \"Checkbox\" labels on rows 2-3 would be the SAME item.\n\nBut then \"Checkbox\" is just a label annotation saying