onsale are next to the image. On row 3, feat/onsale are next to Price. The visual effect is that feat/onsale span the 2nd and 3rd rows, creating a larger area for the checkboxes.\n\nSince feat/onsale have `align-items: center` on the grid container, they'll be vertically centered in the 2-row span. The checkboxes and labels will be centered between row 2 and row 3.\n\nThis could look nice! Let me implement it.\n\nOne thing I need to handle: the `.ml` labels inside feat/onsale. They should still be visible on mobile.\n\nLet me also think about the edit/delete buttons. If I use `display: contents` on td:nth-child(10), the buttons become grid items. But the td also has inline styles. With `display: contents`, those inline styles are ignored (the td is visually removed). That's fine - I'll style the buttons directly in CSS.\n\nLet me implement this now."},{"role":"user","content":"Continue if you have next steps, or stop and ask for clarification if you are unsure how to proceed."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Here's a summary of what we've changed so far:\n\n**1. `admin-page.tsx`** — Moved Title display into the Delete button's `<td>`, so Title text renders inside the delete button container instead of as a separate cell.\n\n**2. `globals.css`** (mobile grid) — Replaced the 4-row grid layout:\n\n| Before | After |\n|---|---|\n| Row 1: img + Title (full width) | Row 1: img + Collection + Year + Status |\n| Row 2: img + Coll + Year + Status | Row 2: img + (empty) + Featured + On Sale |\n| Row 3: Price + (empty) + Featured + On Sale | Row 3: Price + (empty) + *Featured* + *On Sale* (span) |\n| Row 4: Drag + (empty) + Actions (flex row) | Row 4: Drag + (empty) + **Edit** + (empty) + **Delete** |\n\n- Removed Title from grid entirely\n- Featured/On Sale now span rows 2–3\n- Used `display: contents` on the actions `<td>` so Edit and Delete become separate grid items at `edit` (col 3) and `delete` (col 5)\n\n---\n\nNo further steps unless you want adjustments. What's next?"