and update it.\n\nActually, the cleanest fix is:\n1. Use a ref to store flat allArts array (populated in `load()`)\n2. Add `dirtyCount` or `tick` state to force re-render\n3. Fix `toggleField` to use the ref\n\nLet me write the fix. I'll:\n\n1. In `load()`, save `allArtsRef.current = allArts`\n2. Add `const [tick, setTick] = useState(0)` for re-render forcing\n3. Fix `toggleField` to use `allArtsRef.current`\n\nWait, but there's also a problem. The `toggleField` directly mutates state objects (`item[field] = !item[field]`). This is mutating React state directly, which is an anti-pattern. However, since it then forces a re-render and Supabase is the source of truth, it might work... but it's fragile.\n\nA better approach: use Supabase as source of truth. Toggle the field, update Supabase, then reload from Supabase. But that's slow.\n\nThe pragmatic fix: Use a ref to avoid the `allArts` issue, add `tick` state for re-render, and the direct mutation is \"good enough\" for an admin panel.\n\nLet me implement:"},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_00_bEbfYdVWB9jktP9Pmdql8095","content":"Found multiple matches for oldString. Provide more surrounding context to make the match unique."},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_rKlm48JIptGLF0iIl8Xb6090","type":"function","function":{"name":"edit","arguments":"{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Joe\\\\Downloads\\\\Magazine_prototype_backup\\\\app\\\\admin\\\\page.js\",\"newString\":\"function ArtworksManager({ setError, setSuccess }) {\\n  const [grouped, setGrouped] = useState([])\\n  const [uncollected, setUncollected] = useState([])\\n  const [collections, setCollections] = useState([])\\n  const [onSaleArts, setOnSaleArts] = useState([])\\n  const [edit, setEdit] = useState(null)\\n  const [busy, setBusy] = useState(false)\\n  const [dirty, setDirty] = useState(false)\\n  const [tick, setTick] = useState(0)\\n  const dragSrc = useRef(null)\\n  const allArtsRef = useRef([])\",\"oldString\":\"function Artwo